    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="1269" n="1073" xml:id="pg1073"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760h.68/7–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1081<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-28">July 28, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 392. To Acting Secretary of State,
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>Reference your 117, July 24<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1081-f1"/> regarding notes of
                    protest received by the Embassy at Belgrade from the Yugoslav Foreign Office
                    concerning disturbances along the Greek-Yugoslav frontier. I concur in your
                    belief that this situation can best be solved by an on the spot investigation of
                    the Yugoslav charges. I do not believe that it is desirable to send a special
                    mission into this area. Therefore your proposed reply should be amended to
                    indicate that we are prepared to recommend the appointment of a commission
                    composed of military and political representatives drawn from the present staffs
                    of the American, British and Soviet missions in Belgrade and the American and
                    British missions in Athens. It would be necessary for the Soviet Government to
                    appoint a special group to collaborate with the Athens group. With this
                    clarification I agree that you should proceed to take immediate action on this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
